      "side": 1,
      "message": "The mutable executor here means that our current api for registerConnectivityDiagnosticsCallback() still works.\n\nIf we want to avoid the mutability here, we can try to have a static Map\u003cConnectivityDiagnosticsBinder, Executor\u003e. However, this means we will be using strong references on the IBinders, so app deaths won\u0027t trigger the Binder.DeathRecipient behavior in ConnectivityService (defined in aosp/1200998). We can use WeakReference\u003cConnectivityDiagnosticsBinder\u003e, but these don\u0027t override hashCode() so storing them in an easily accessible way gets tricky.\n\nThese approach seems to be the best compromise immediately available from what I can tell. Thoughts?",
